dsn-title = Delivery status report
dsn-unverified = This report describes the sender's delivery attempt. Its claims are not independently verified. Delivery does not mean the message was read.
dsn-reporting-mta = Reporting server:
dsn-original-recipient = Original recipient:
dsn-remote-mta = Remote server:
dsn-last-attempt = Last attempt:
dsn-retry-until = Sender plans to retry until:
dsn-action-failed = Reported failure
dsn-action-delayed = Reported delay
dsn-action-delivered = Reported delivery
dsn-action-relayed = Reported relay
dsn-action-expanded = Reported list expansion

# Enhanced SMTP status meanings; IANA registry, checked 2026-11-09.
dsn-status-0-0 = The server did not give a more specific reason.
dsn-status-1-0 = There is a problem with an email address.
dsn-status-1-1 = The recipient mailbox does not exist. Confirm the address with the recipient.
dsn-status-1-2 = The recipient domain cannot receive this mail. Check the part after @.
dsn-status-1-3 = The recipient address has an invalid format. Check for typos or extra spaces.
dsn-status-1-4 = The server cannot identify a unique recipient for this address.
dsn-status-1-5 = The recipient address was accepted as valid.
dsn-status-1-6 = This mailbox has moved and no forwarding address is available. Ask for the new address.
dsn-status-1-7 = The sender address has an invalid format. Check the account's sending address.
dsn-status-1-8 = The sender domain is invalid or cannot receive return mail.
dsn-status-1-9 = The message was handed to a system that cannot provide further delivery reports.
dsn-status-1-10 = The recipient domain explicitly declares that it accepts no email (null MX). Use another address.
dsn-status-2-0 = The recipient mailbox has an unspecified problem.
dsn-status-2-1 = The recipient mailbox is disabled or is not accepting messages. Contact the recipient another way.
dsn-status-2-2 = The recipient mailbox is full. The recipient needs to free space or increase their quota.
dsn-status-2-3 = The message exceeds this recipient's size limit. Reduce attachments or use a sharing link.
dsn-status-2-4 = The server could not resolve the members of a mailing list. Contact the list owner.
dsn-status-3-0 = The receiving mail system reported an unspecified problem.
dsn-status-3-1 = The receiving mail server has run out of storage. Its administrator needs to free space.
dsn-status-3-2 = The receiving server is not accepting mail, for example during maintenance or overload.
dsn-status-3-3 = The receiving system does not support a feature required by this message.
dsn-status-3-4 = The message exceeds the receiving server's size limit. Reduce attachments or use a sharing link.
dsn-status-3-5 = A mail server configuration problem prevents delivery. Ask the mail administrator to investigate.
dsn-status-3-6 = The server accepted the message but changed its requested delivery priority.
dsn-status-4-0 = A network or mail-routing problem was reported without further detail.
dsn-status-4-1 = The receiving server did not answer the connection attempt.
dsn-status-4-2 = The connection was established but interrupted before the mail transfer finished.
dsn-status-4-3 = A DNS or directory lookup failed. A mail administrator may need to check name resolution.
dsn-status-4-4 = The server could not find a route to the recipient's mail system.
dsn-status-4-5 = Mail traffic congestion prevented delivery.
dsn-status-4-6 = A forwarding loop was detected. Ask the administrator to check forwarding and routing rules.
dsn-status-4-7 = The delivery time limit expired. Check the diagnostic for the underlying problem before resending.
dsn-status-5-0 = The mail servers could not complete their delivery protocol exchange.
dsn-status-5-1 = A mail server rejected an unsupported command or a command sent in the wrong order.
dsn-status-5-2 = A mail server could not understand the syntax of a command.
dsn-status-5-3 = The message has too many recipients. Send to smaller groups.
dsn-status-5-4 = A mail server rejected the parameters of a command.
dsn-status-5-5 = The servers use incompatible versions of the mail protocol.
dsn-status-5-6 = The authentication response was too long for the server. Ask the mail administrator to check authentication settings.
dsn-status-6-0 = The server reported an unspecified problem with the message content or format.
dsn-status-6-1 = The receiving system does not support this message's content type.
dsn-status-6-2 = Delivery requires a content conversion that the sender or server policy forbids.
dsn-status-6-3 = Delivery requires a content conversion that the server cannot perform.
dsn-status-6-4 = A content conversion lost some information. Check the original message and the server diagnostic.
dsn-status-6-5 = The server failed while converting the message content.
dsn-status-6-6 = The server could not retrieve the message content from another system.
dsn-status-6-7 = An international email address is not supported for this sender or recipient. Ask for an alternative address.
dsn-status-6-8 = The server needs an international (UTF-8) reply that the sending system cannot accept.
dsn-status-6-9 = The message contains international (UTF-8) headers that cannot be delivered to at least one recipient.
dsn-status-6-10 = This obsolete code means an international (UTF-8) reply is required but unsupported, as with code x.6.8.
dsn-status-7-0 = A security rule or mail policy prevented normal delivery. Check the server diagnostic for the exact rule.
dsn-status-7-1 = The server refused permission to deliver, possibly because of filtering or relay restrictions. Ask the mail administrator to check the diagnostic.
dsn-status-7-2 = The sender is not allowed to post to this mailing list. Contact the list owner.
dsn-status-7-3 = Delivery requires a security-format conversion that the server cannot perform.
dsn-status-7-4 = The delivery system does not support a required security feature.
dsn-status-7-5 = The server could not validate or decrypt the message, for example because a key was missing or invalid.
dsn-status-7-6 = The server does not support a cryptographic algorithm required by the message.
dsn-status-7-7 = An integrity check indicates that the message was changed or damaged.
dsn-status-7-8 = The sending server rejected the login credentials. Check the account's authentication settings.
dsn-status-7-9 = The authentication method is weaker than the server allows. A stronger method is required.
dsn-status-7-10 = The server requires an encrypted connection or stronger protection before authentication.
dsn-status-7-11 = This authentication method requires an encrypted SMTP connection (TLS).
dsn-status-7-12 = The account needs an authentication-method or password migration. Contact the account provider.
dsn-status-7-13 = The sending account is disabled. Contact its administrator to restore access.
dsn-status-7-14 = The server needs a configured trust relationship to retrieve the message. Contact its administrator.
dsn-status-7-15 = The message priority is below the receiving server's current minimum.
dsn-status-7-16 = The message is too large for its requested priority. Reduce its size or ask the administrator.
dsn-status-7-17 = The recipient mailbox has changed ownership since the required date. Confirm the recipient before sending again.
dsn-status-7-18 = The recipient domain has changed ownership since the required date. Confirm the destination before sending again.
dsn-status-7-19 = The server could not verify continuous ownership of the recipient address. Ask the administrator about the recipient-validity check.
dsn-status-7-20 = No DKIM signature passed verification. Ask the sender's mail administrator to check signing and DNS.
dsn-status-7-21 = A DKIM signature passed, but the receiving server's policy did not accept it.
dsn-status-7-22 = No accepted DKIM signature matched the From address. Ask the mail administrator to check signing-domain alignment.
dsn-status-7-23 = SPF failed: the sending server was not authorized by the sender domain's SPF policy.
dsn-status-7-24 = The server encountered an error while checking SPF. Ask the mail administrator to check SPF records and DNS.
dsn-status-7-25 = The sending server failed the receiver's reverse-DNS check. Its administrator needs to check the IP address's DNS records.
dsn-status-7-26 = Multiple message-authentication checks failed. The diagnostic may identify SPF, DKIM, or DMARC policy problems.
dsn-status-7-27 = The sender domain declares that it accepts no return email (null MX), which the receiver rejects.
dsn-status-7-28 = The receiving system detected a possible flood of abusive messages.
dsn-status-7-29 = ARC verification failed, so the receiver could not accept the message's recorded authentication chain.
dsn-status-7-30 = The message requires REQUIRETLS, but the next mail server does not support it. Ask the administrator to check secure delivery support.

dsn-class-2 = Success: the server reports a positive delivery step. This does not prove the message was read.
dsn-class-4 = Temporary failure: a later attempt may succeed. A delay report may still be retried by the sender; a failure report means that attempt has ended.
dsn-class-5 = Permanent failure: resending the same message unchanged is unlikely to work. Correct the cause before sending again.
dsn-category-0 = The server supplied an unrecognized or provider-specific detail code. Its diagnostic below may explain the exact cause.
dsn-category-1 = This is an address-related code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-2 = This is a recipient-mailbox code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-3 = This is a receiving-mail-system code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-4 = This is a network or routing code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-5 = This is a mail-protocol code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-6 = This is a message-content or format code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized.
dsn-category-7 = This is a security or policy code. The precise detail is provider-specific or not recognized; it does not by itself establish that the message is spam.
dsn-advice-success = Check the reported delivery action above for whether the message was delivered, relayed, or expanded to a list.
dsn-advice-0 = Use the server diagnostic when asking your email provider for help.
dsn-advice-1 = Check both sender and recipient addresses. Confirm the recipient's current address if necessary.
dsn-advice-2 = Contact the recipient another way if the mailbox problem persists.
dsn-advice-3 = Share this report with the receiving mail system's administrator if the problem persists.
dsn-advice-4 = Ask your mail administrator to check connectivity, DNS, and forwarding routes if the problem persists.
dsn-advice-5 = Share the diagnostic with your email provider so they can check SMTP compatibility and limits.
dsn-advice-6 = Check the message format, international addresses, and attachments against the receiver's requirements.
dsn-advice-7 = Share the diagnostic with your mail administrator to identify the exact security or authentication rule.
dsn-meaning-title = What this code means
dsn-next-step = What to do
dsn-server-diagnostic = Server diagnostic

# Provider-specific interpretations; official references are linked in the report.
dsn-vendor-exchange-generic = Exchange reported a general delivery rejection. The diagnostic identifies the actual issue, which may involve message formatting or attachment policy.
dsn-vendor-exchange-recipient = Exchange could not resolve this recipient in its directory. Check the address and remove any outdated autocomplete entry before creating a new message.
dsn-vendor-exchange-sender-blocked = Microsoft restricted this sending account after detecting suspected spam or abuse. This may require an administrator to secure and unblock the account.
dsn-vendor-headers = The receiving service rejected invalid or missing message headers. The sending application needs to generate correctly formatted mail.
dsn-vendor-sending-limit = The sending account has exceeded a message or recipient quota. Repeated immediate resends will not remove the limit.
dsn-vendor-exchange-recipient-rate = Exchange has received too many messages from this sender to this recipient within its hourly window.
dsn-vendor-exchange-receive-rate = This Exchange recipient has reached the hourly receiving limit across all senders.
dsn-vendor-exchange-journaling = The organization is trying to journal on-premises messages into Microsoft 365 without the required archive configuration.
dsn-vendor-exchange-recipient-access = Exchange rejected access to this recipient or destination domain. Check the recipient address and the organization's accepted-domain configuration.
dsn-vendor-routing-loop = The message entered a forwarding or routing loop and exceeded the permitted number of hops.
dsn-vendor-expired = The sending service gave up after its delivery time window expired. Check the diagnostic for the connection or routing failure that caused the delay.
dsn-vendor-exchange-internal-only = This Exchange recipient accepts authenticated senders from its own organization; this message was treated as external or unauthenticated.
dsn-vendor-exchange-public-folder = This Exchange public folder does not accept this external or unauthenticated sender.
dsn-vendor-exchange-auth = The application or device did not authenticate correctly for Microsoft 365 SMTP submission.
dsn-vendor-exchange-connector = Microsoft could not authorize the relay through the configured tenant connector. Its certificate, sending IP, or accepted domain may no longer match.
dsn-vendor-exchange-group-allow = The sender is not in this Exchange group's permitted-senders list.
dsn-vendor-exchange-group-internal = This Exchange distribution group rejects senders outside its organization unless its owner or administrator permits them.
dsn-vendor-exchange-tenant-limit = The Microsoft 365 organization has reached its rolling daily limit for external recipients.
dsn-vendor-exchange-onmicrosoft-limit = The organization reached the external-recipient limit for its onmicrosoft.com sending domain. Regular sending should use a verified custom domain.
dsn-vendor-exchange-forward-relay = A downstream system rejected forwarded or relayed mail. Authentication may have been affected by forwarding or a non-Microsoft gateway.
dsn-vendor-helo = The sending server used an unacceptable HELO/EHLO identity. Its greeting must identify the sending server correctly.
dsn-vendor-recipient-ip-block = The recipient organization explicitly blocks the sending IP address. Its administrator controls this local block.
dsn-vendor-dmarc = The receiver's DMARC policy was not satisfied. Check SPF or DKIM authentication and alignment with the visible From domain.
dsn-vendor-exchange-ipv6 = The destination does not accept this delivery over IPv6. The sending administrator needs to check the route or use an accepted transport.
dsn-vendor-ip-block = The receiving service rejected the sending IP because of its reputation or a blocklist entry.
dsn-vendor-exchange-forwarding = Microsoft 365 policy blocks automatic forwarding to external recipients. The organization's administrator must review the forwarding policy.
dsn-vendor-exchange-tenant-blocklist = A recipient address or domain is blocked by the sender organization's Tenant Allow/Block List. One blocked destination can reject the entire message.
dsn-vendor-exchange-tenant-blocked = Microsoft restricted sending for this organization because its traffic was considered suspicious.
dsn-vendor-exchange-unregistered = Microsoft rejected sending from a domain that is not properly registered and verified in the tenant.
dsn-vendor-exchange-domain-blocked = Microsoft restricted this sending domain after detecting suspected spam activity.
dsn-vendor-exchange-temporary-restriction = Microsoft is temporarily restricting this sending IP or traffic while evaluating suspicious activity.
dsn-vendor-mta-sts-host = The destination mail server is not permitted by the domain's MTA-STS policy.
dsn-vendor-connection-refused = The destination server refused the network connection. Its mail service, firewall, or network route needs checking.
dsn-vendor-certificate-chain = The remote TLS certificate could not be validated against the required trust or MTA-STS policy.
dsn-vendor-starttls = The required encrypted SMTP connection could not be established or was not supported by the next server.
dsn-vendor-certificate-expired = The destination mail server presented an expired TLS certificate.
dsn-vendor-dane = The destination's TLS certificate or TLSA configuration did not satisfy DANE validation.
dsn-vendor-dnssec = The destination domain's DNSSEC records could not be validated.
dsn-vendor-certificate-host = The destination TLS certificate does not match the required mail-server hostname.
dsn-vendor-gmail-browser-login = Google requires an account sign-in or security check in the browser before allowing this SMTP login.
dsn-vendor-gmail-spf-record = Google considers the sender domain's SPF configuration invalid or suspicious.
dsn-vendor-ptr = The sending IP lacks acceptable reverse DNS, or its PTR name does not resolve back to the same IP.
dsn-vendor-gmail-authentication = Google did not accept the sender's authentication. The diagnostic distinguishes missing SPF/DKIM, SPF hard failure, and DMARC rejection.
dsn-vendor-spf = The receiver did not accept SPF authentication for the sending IP and envelope-sender domain.
dsn-vendor-gmail-rate = Google applied a sending or relay limit, or detected an unusual message rate. The diagnostic identifies the affected account, IP, or domain.
dsn-vendor-dkim = The receiver did not accept the message's DKIM authentication or signing configuration.
dsn-vendor-credentials = The SMTP service rejected the supplied login credentials.
dsn-vendor-gmail-app-password = Google requires an app password or a supported account authorization method for this SMTP login.
dsn-vendor-gmail-custom-policy = A Google Workspace administrator's custom mail rule rejected the message. This does not necessarily mean Google's spam filter rejected it.
dsn-vendor-gmail-auth-method = Google rejected an unsupported authentication method, such as the retired XOAUTH method.
dsn-vendor-gmail-dmarc-record = Google requires a DMARC record with a declared policy for this sending domain.
dsn-vendor-gmail-reputation = Google's filtering rejected the message because it considered the mail unsolicited or the sending IP/domain reputation too low.
dsn-vendor-content-security = The gateway rejected message content or an attachment under its security filtering rules. Consult its diagnostic or logs for the specific item.
dsn-vendor-gmail-relay = Google Workspace did not authorize the sending IP, domain, or account for its SMTP relay service.
dsn-vendor-mimecast-spoof = Mimecast's anti-spoofing policy rejected the sender identity.
dsn-vendor-mimecast-block = Mimecast rejected the sender or domain under a blocked-sender or administrative policy.
dsn-vendor-mimecast-content = A Mimecast content-examination policy rejected the message.
dsn-vendor-proofpoint-throttle = Proofpoint temporarily deferred this sending IP because its sending pattern was considered unusual.
dsn-vendor-proofpoint-block = Proofpoint blocked the sending IP or domain after detecting spam or malicious activity.
dsn-vendor-barracuda-reputation = Barracuda's reputation service lists or blocks the sending IP address.
dsn-vendor-fortimail-relay = FortiMail denied this delivery under its access-control or relay policy. The gateway administrator needs to check the matching receiving rule.
dsn-vendor-relay = The mail server will not relay this message to the destination. Check SMTP authentication, trusted sending IPs, connectors, and accepted domains.
dsn-vendor-greylist = The gateway temporarily deferred this delivery using greylisting. A correctly configured sending server normally retries later.
dsn-vendor-yahoo-deferred = Yahoo temporarily deferred this message, commonly while evaluating volume, reputation, or recipient complaints. Check the diagnostic for the stated cause.
dsn-vendor-yahoo-policy = Yahoo rejected the message under its mail policy. Authentication, DMARC alignment, or message content may be involved; the diagnostic gives the specific reason.
dsn-vendor-advice-account = Ask the sending administrator to investigate possible account abuse, secure the account, and request removal of the restriction.
dsn-vendor-advice-admin = Share this diagnostic with the organization's mail administrator to review the matching configuration or policy.
dsn-vendor-advice-format = Ask the sending application or mail administrator to correct message generation, then create a fresh message.
dsn-vendor-advice-rate = Reduce sending volume and wait for the quota or restriction to clear. Check the reported action before assuming this attempt is still queued.
dsn-vendor-advice-route = Ask the mail administrator to check the destination, forwarding rules, mail service, and firewall/network path.
dsn-vendor-advice-recipient-admin = Contact the recipient or group owner another way and ask their administrator to review the relevant permission or policy.
dsn-vendor-advice-auth = Check the account's supported SMTP authentication method and authorization. Complete any required sign-in through the provider's official account page.
dsn-vendor-advice-connector = Ask the administrator to check relay authorization, connector IP/certificate matching, accepted domains, and the actual mail route.
dsn-vendor-advice-domain = Ask the Microsoft 365 administrator to register and verify the sending domain and review the tenant's sending limits.
dsn-vendor-advice-dns = Ask the sending mail administrator or IP provider to correct DNS, reverse DNS, and the SMTP server identity.
dsn-vendor-advice-authentication = Ask the sender's administrator to check SPF, DKIM, DMARC, and domain alignment using the exact diagnostic.
dsn-vendor-advice-reputation = Ask the sending administrator to investigate unwanted traffic and reputation, then follow the provider's official review or delisting process.
dsn-vendor-advice-tls = Ask the mail administrators to repair TLS, certificates, or DNS security records so the required secure route can succeed.
dsn-vendor-advice-content = Review the diagnostic and gateway logs with the recipient's administrator to identify the blocked content and the applicable policy.
